SCENARIO 3: Deadline and grace enforcement on both bash versions
Generated by live validation against real product (bin/fm-timeout-lib.sh)

Date: 2026-09-30T14:34:09Z
Host: perl 5.42.2, no GNU timeout (perl watchdog path only), as on stock macOS

=== /bin/bash (3.2.57) ===
Version: GNU bash, version 3.2.57(1)-release (arm64-apple-darwin25)
PERL_DIR=/opt/homebrew/bin

--- 3a: cooperative command should end at bound (1s), not grace (30s) ---
Method: ( . fm-timeout-lib.sh; PATH=$PERL_DIR:/bin:/usr/bin fm_exec_timed 1 30 bash -c 'exec sleep 300' )
rc=124 elapsed=1s expected 124 ~1s
PASS 3a cooperative: TERM sent at bound, command ended before grace

--- 3b: TERM-ignoring command killed after grace (1s + 2s grace => ~3s) ---
Method: trap "" TERM; fm_exec_timed 1 2 ...
rc=124 elapsed=3s expected 124 ~3s
PASS 3b ignoring: KILL sent after grace, command killed

